In goldenland-realestate-v2, the issue-tracker workflow is a user preference — missing it gets called out: keep a clean working tree, run the full test suite, commit with a clear message, then close the ticket via `gh issue close` with a summary comment; append a context pointer to parent issue #1's 'Implementation Decisions' section (format: commit SHA, review ledger path, issue closure date). The code-review skill runs as a mandatory step before committing — two-axis review (Standards/Spec) in parallel sub-agents, findings fixed before commit; it reviews uncommitted work against a fixed point (HEAD) with the originating issue as spec source, findings saved to `docs/agents/reviews/<issue-number>.md`. `.pi-subagents/` is pi-generated noise and must be gitignored. <!-- created=2026-08-06, last=2026-08-07 -->
